WEBVTT

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:46.000
<b>{Episode 4:
A Place to Be, a Place to Call Home!</b>

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.290
If it's a pain, change it.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.720
Little One Inch!

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.100
There you go.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:06.940
Well?

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:09.860
Have you figured out what you need to picture 
in your mind for Buchhülle to work?

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.020
Maybe I have!

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:15.020
<i>There's one month until the Hexennacht.</i>

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.820
<i>I can't cause trouble for Shizuka-chan.</i>

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:23.280
<i>I want to go to the Hexennacht with her!</i>

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:26.370
So I'm going to make this Buchhülle...

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.290
...succeed!

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.730
That's no good.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:34.720
Why are you here?

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:35.420
Are you a spy?

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:38.590
The Coalition is our enemy.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:42.260
Why would I be spying on her?

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.450
True enough.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.310
I'm just bored.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.560
Sis!

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:50.890
You guys!

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.610
Charles!

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.360
The fighters aren't supposed to be here yet!

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.660
I came here because 
I couldn't wait to see you!

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.740
To Japan!

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.650
Across the sea!

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:07.430
Ow!

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:10.710
I keep telling you not to make up silly lies.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:13.040
You didn't need to hit so hard!

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.630
Qazan's teammates.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.960
You guys are so bad with directions

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:24.160
that when I said to get me a drink,
 you didn't come back for three days.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.060
I don't know how you made it here.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:29.350
What's up, Molly?

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.110
Um, actually...

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.230
I brought them here.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.690
Hey there, Qazan-chan.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:40.030
<i>Who is she...</i>

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:42.820
Why are you two working 
with someone like her?!

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:47.240
They were trying to hitchhike to Japan!

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:51.210
<b>Japan</b>

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:51.220
I thought that if I let them alone, 
they'd shrivel up and die before they got here,

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.400
so I brought them here.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.350
Anyway, no greeting 
after this touching reunion?

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:58.630
How mean!

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.000
I'm Lynne Daves from the American school.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.430
H-Hi, there.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:14.470
Nice to meet you, Kagimura Hazuki-san.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:17.270
U-Um... How do you know my name?

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.270
Of course I know your name!

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:22.210
You're the girl who made a contract 
with the famous Cinderella!

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:25.610
The long-missing Origin was 
in the hands of a girl from Japan,

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:29.240
and from the other world, too!

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:31.230
Where did you find it?

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.210
How did you make that contract?

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.420
That's enough.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:41.550
The schools participating in the main 
Hexennacht have a lot to do, right?

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:42.690
Too bad.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.540
See you later, then!

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.400
Um... Thank you...

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.560
Um...

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.900
Stop it.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.270
I didn't get rid of her for your sake.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:00.900
<i>Qazan-san might actually be really nice.</i>

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.610
Who's this?

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:04.970
Is she our new member?

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:07.570
No, she's from the Japanese school.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.160
So she's an enemy!

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:13.570
The Japanese school 
is giving me everything I need

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:16.270
because I'm an exchange student.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.400
First, you should thank her.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:19.980
Right!

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.010
Thanks!

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:22.390
Thank you.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.340
I didn't do anything...

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:25.920
What?

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.090
Then she really is an enemy!

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.860
I said stop!

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:30.870
Sorry.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:33.020
They're idiots and really single-minded.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.820
They go out of control quickly.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:40.230
Sis, in Japan, the girl who calls 
someone stupid is the one who's stupid!

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:43.900
Which means that you're stupid!

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:47.740
So... Since you just called me stupid, 
what does that make you?

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.590
H-Huh?

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:54.000
I said you're stupid, 
so it's not me who's stupid.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:59.720
It's you who's stupid, 
but since I said that, I'm stupid...

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:02.090
I don't know anymore!

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:02.860
See?

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:04.080
They're stupid.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.880
The only cure for stupidity is death.

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:11.220
Hey, Molly! Sis is one thing, 
but I don't want to hear that from you!

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:13.910
I keep telling you not to fight!

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:18.020
You three are really friends, huh?

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:32.140
<i>When will I be able to transform?</i>

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:36.260
<i>Can I be useful to Shizuka-chan like this?</i>

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:39.890
<i>Maybe it's impossible for 
someone like me to be a witch...</i>

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:43.840
No, no!

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.800
Hazuki-san?

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:48.800
Shizuka-chan!

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:50.570
I didn't think I'd get to see you today!

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:54.640
Maria Rasputin.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:56.680
I'm the leader of the Russian school.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:01.790
Meetings with the team leaders, 
with the committee...

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:04.610
Tsuchimikado Shizuka is quite busy.

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:07.040
I'm Kagimura Hazuki.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:07.610
I see.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:08.770
You're the one, huh?

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:12.110
I'd never have thought Cinderella 
was at the Japanese school.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:15.630
It originally belonged 
to my fatherland, Russia.

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:17.200
It did?

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:23.530
In most cases, it's not clear where 
and when a certain story was born.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:26.170
That goes for more than just Cinderella.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:29.190
So, Comrade Hazuki Kagimura.

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:32.090
Come to my school, 
and bring your Origin with you.

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:33.050
Maria...

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:35.140
I heard that.

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:39.280
All wisdom travels down 
the pure waters of the Ganges,

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:41.500
and reaches the holy land of Rishikesh.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:46.220
In other words, all stories 
belong to the Indian school.

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:51.420
No, wisdom travels to the top of Mt. Penglai.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:57.960
Um... You're Mahakali of the Indian school,

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:00.580
and Li Xuemei of the Chinese school, right?

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.210
And then, behind you is...

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:06.860
U-Um, everyone, I want to go 
to the Hexennacht with Shizuka-chan.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:08.350
S-So... U-Um...

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:09.420
I'm sorry.

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:11.520
Don't worry.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:14.940
The Chinese school is prepared 
to take not just Cinderella,

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:16.890
but the Moon Princess as well.

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:24.820
Sorry!

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:28.200
I didn't mean to. My hand just slipped.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:31.300
But I don't think it's right 
to try and get a leg up like that.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:32.730
Lynne Daves.

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:34.960
You've got guts, going after the boss.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:36.500
If that's what you want...

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.230
Stop it, Xuelan.

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:40.490
You mustn't fall for her provocation.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:44.740
I've heard that the American 
school is toying with the stories

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:48.710
and Origins in a rather unpleasant way.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:52.630
Judging by your attitude, 
I guess the rumors must be true.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:55.620
"Toying with" is such a rude way to put it.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:59.430
Composite Origins. Call it mixed media.

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:04.100
<i>Her Origin is the Little Match Girl?</i>

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:07.420
You want to fight my Journey to the West?

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:08.190
Magical Wand!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:15.110
The American and Chinese schools

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:19.220
think they're the only ones 
in the world who matter.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.080
Don't forget the Russian school.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:25.760
Indeed. The Russian girl is right.

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:29.790
Americans are newcomers. 
I can't let you show off.

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:33.630
Don't fight here!

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:35.590
This isn't a fight.

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:36.800
It's just a brawl.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.030
A brawl? No, no.

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:41.310
This is a one-sided beating.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:42.430
Shut up!

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:47.610
Basho Fan!

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:54.310
Hazuki-san, run!

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:56.030
Hurry!

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:09.790
W-Was this place this big?

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.670
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:16.940
Bad monkey.

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:28.120
How did this happen?

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:29.200
A flea.

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:30.760
Just kidding.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:31.790
Um...

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:34.360
Why are you here?

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:38.130
Th-There was a fight over there,

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:40.270
so I thought I'd come here instead.

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:41.560
You ran, didn't you?

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:45.510
I can't use my Buchhülle,

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:48.330
and I can't fight like 
Shizuka-chan and the others.

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:50.120
So you ran.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.040
I...

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.120
Yes.

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:53.890
You're trying hard.

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:55.450
You're trying to change.

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:57.510
But you're scared to change.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.430
You keep running...

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:03.390
From reality, from yourself...

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:05.600
From everything you don't like.

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:10.770
Wh-Why are you saying that?

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:12.600
You're...

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.240
How far will you run?

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.790
Knock this off!

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:40.740
Boss!

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:45.640
Looks like the yellow match 
finally took effect.

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:48.100
What did you do?

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:50.150
You wanna know?

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:52.560
But I won't tell you!

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:56.320
So lame!

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:58.090
What happened?

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.360
Wh-What's going on?

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:07.690
When did she...

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:11.580
W-Wait!

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:16.980
That Basho Fan is the worst thing 
you could have against my matches.

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:20.420
So I'm going to have you disappear now.

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:21.800
Don't hate me, okay?

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.220
N-No!

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.180
Bye-bye!

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:40.570
What? Don't get in my way.

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:43.240
The fewer rivals, the better, right?

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:46.200
I don't like that way of doing things.

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:47.460
Right, right.

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:48.970
Forget it.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:51.350
Hmph!

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:54.620
That's so boring.

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:05.840
Once the poison on your skin's been 
washed off, you'll be able to move.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:17.730
Hazuki-san?

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:34.270
<i>I had no idea she was strong...</i>

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:38.560
<i>She was here as an exchange student,</i>

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:41.320
<i>so I never paid attention to her.</i>

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:44.200
<i>If only we could get enough people,</i>

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:46.010
<i>if only we could get a chance to participate,</i>

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:48.720
<i>the Coalition would be 
no match for us, I thought.</i>

00:13:56.590 --> 00:13:58.400
<i>But that incredible resolve...</i>

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:02.910
<i>Is it okay to put Hazuki-san against her?</i>

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:05.430
I-I'm sorry, Shizuka-chan.

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:09.420
I'm sorry all I do is run...

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.280
I'll get back to practice.

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:14.750
You mustn't force yourself.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:18.990
U-Um...

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:19.630
Yes?

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:23.460
I heard famous Maedchens 
have lots of fans, right?

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.690
Yes, so I've heard.

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:28.260
I don't really know myself...

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:29.570
A-And so...

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:34.150
There was a profile of you 
on the Hexennacht site...

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:35.570
And, um...

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:37.850
Your birthday's coming up, isn't it?

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:41.240
So how about we have a party?

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:43.110
I'll cook something!

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.940
We can have Ariko-san 
and the principal come...

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:48.820
Would Qazan-san come?

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:53.540
Anyway, it's wonderful that 
your birthday is on Christmas!

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:54.550
I'll never forget itー

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:55.120
Stop it!

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:57.710
I'm sorry...

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.540
I'll be going.

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:05.000
What happened?

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:06.320
Oh, no...

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:08.920
I made Shizuka-chan mad!

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:18.430
So that's it, huh?

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:22.150
Did I say something bad to her?

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:23.630
Well...

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:28.440
Her mom died on her birthday.

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:35.530
Hey, there!

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:39.080
You're late!

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:41.910
I'm busy, you know?

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:44.820
Interviews, magazine articles, photo shoots...

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:46.800
It's really hard being famous.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.350
You're the one who called me here.

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:50.510
Right, right.

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:57.180
Thanks, like always.

00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:01.950
By the way, that was some 
great acting back there.

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:03.410
After all that,

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:08.400
nobody will ever think you 
and I are working behind the scenes.

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:10.110
It's a disgusting way of doing things.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:12.770
Are you one to talk?

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:14.880
You're using your position 
as an exchange student

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:18.160
to get information on all the other schools.

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.750
That face!

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:24.850
Hey, were you, maybe, really serious 
about trying to kill me back there?

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:30.290
Since you already hate me, 
how about I ask you for one more thing?

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:33.300
Can you knock that Cinderella 
girl out of the picture?

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:37.980
There are actually some plans 
to get rid of the Japanese school.

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:38.970
What?

00:16:39.190 --> 00:16:42.250
This country lost a lot of Origin Wielders

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:45.190
in the fight with the magical 
beasts seven years ago, right?

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:48.790
On December 25th, seven years ago,

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:53.900
a unbelievably huge magical beast, 
a Fleck, appeared in Japan.

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:59.200
It was more powerful than any 
in the last several centuries...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.020
A Fleck...

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:05.370
Shizuka's mother fought it, and died.

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:08.840
This is what the Committee of 13 thinks.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:14.430
This country doesn't have the strength 
left to protect an Origin Library.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:19.910
So wouldn't it be better 
to distribute its valuable Origins

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:22.330
to the other schools 
before the Flecks eat them?

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:24.850
That's the plan.

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:27.400
And if that happens,

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:31.070
we'll be given priority 
to receive the Origins.

00:17:31.390 --> 00:17:36.280
Shizuka-san's mom was so busy, 
she was almost never home.

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:40.520
So Shizuka was really 
looking forward to the call

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:42.750
her mother made on her birthday.

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:47.880
I guess she spent the whole day 
waiting for a call that would never come...

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:51.210
<i>The day her mother died...</i>

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:56.680
<i>I know how painful those memories are.</i>

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:02.790
<i>It's a lie that time heals 
the wounds of the heart.</i>

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:04.100
<i>But...</i>

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:07.170
I...

00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:09.690
I said something so awful to her!

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:11.770
It's not your fault, Hazuki.

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:17.910
Sis gets a really nice room, huh?

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:19.710
The Japanese school's amazing.

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:21.070
I'm jealous.

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:25.590
The girls in the Japanese school 
have a place to call home.

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:33.200
We'll have one, too. Someday.

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:40.890
Shizuka-chan?

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:43.810
Um...

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:45.270
Shuten-Doji.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:52.440
Q-Qazan-san?

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:06.030
Qazan-san, why?

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:10.080
When you've got a book 
as powerful as Cinderella,

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:12.500
it's gonna be tough to get.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:15.850
There are people out there 
who say stupid stuff,

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:19.970
like respecting the will of the contractor 
or the rights of the individual.

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:24.930
So I want that Origin to be free while I can.

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:28.130
Don't forget your promise.

00:19:28.130 --> 00:19:30.140
I'll help you.

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:33.970
And in exchange, you'll give me what I want.

00:19:33.970 --> 00:19:35.360
A home?

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:42.160
You're a bother!

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:45.490
Getting involved in the Hexennacht 
like it's some kind of game!

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:48.680
<i>Sh-Shizuka-chan, help me!</i>

00:19:58.750 --> 00:19:59.420
Your Origin.

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:04.430
Do your Buchhülle.

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:07.180
Use the power of Cinderella to destroy me.

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:12.850
Hazuki-san!

00:20:13.470 --> 00:20:17.070
I-I know you're really a nice girl...

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:22.260
<i>I was wrong...</i>

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:25.490
<i>It was a mistake to get Hazuki-san 
involved in the Hexennacht...</i>

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:29.370
Dragon's Jaw!

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:35.250
Shizuka-chan!

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:38.340
That was quite the elaborate plot, huh?

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:41.260
Is this why you got close to us!

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.360
I couldn't say.

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:43.970
Imagine what you like.

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:46.180
Hazuki-san!

00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:48.770
I'm sorry...

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:50.940
If I'd been paying more attention...

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:54.100
No, it's not your fault.

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:06.350
Return to your world.

00:21:12.190 --> 00:21:14.920
And never come back, please.

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:18.450
This isn't where you belong.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:22.560
Shizuka-chan, I-I'll do my best,

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:24.340
so don't say that...

00:21:24.870 --> 00:21:27.670
We're f-friends, right?

00:21:29.440 --> 00:21:33.100
I'm not your friend.

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:06.900
<b>Preview Bath</b>

00:23:06.350 --> 00:23:07.160
It's me, Hazuki!

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:07.960
It's me, Arthur.

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:09.790
The world's about to be destroyed?

00:23:09.790 --> 00:23:11.120
Chuuni-byou out of nowhere!

00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:13.830
And the "I can see things which aren't there"
 type that's specific to girls!

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:16.820
We are warriors of light 
who fought in a past life!

00:23:16.820 --> 00:23:18.270
And past lives, too!

00:23:18.270 --> 00:23:19.760
I'm so excited!

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:22.040
And in my last life, our names 
was Yoshida and Takahashi!

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:23.260
It's extremely normal!

00:23:23.260 --> 00:23:25.850
Now, Tanaka, predict the future!

00:23:25.850 --> 00:23:28.240
Next time: "Farewell, My Magic."

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:34.930
<b>Episode 5: 
Farewell, My Magic.</b>

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:30.070
Wait! My name just changed!

00:23:30.070 --> 00:23:31.760
Let us meet again in the next life.

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:40.230
<b>Illustration: Muchimaro</b>
